Make location actually arrive, and say why when it does not

The watch asked for high accuracy only. On a phone indoors that can hang
indefinitely while a coarse network fix would return in a second. It now
fires getCurrentPosition at low accuracy alongside the precise watch and
draws whichever lands first, with a guard so a late coarse fix cannot
overwrite a good GPS one.

It also checks the Permissions API up front, so a site that is already
blocked says so immediately instead of spinning for thirty seconds, and
checks isSecureContext. The waiting state shows secure-page, permission
and in-a-frame values so a failure can be reported precisely.

